    {
      "id": "smy8474",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO ENVIRONMENT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The environment consists of interacting biotic (living) and abiotic (non-living) components.",
        "Natural resources are categorized into renewable (replenishable) and non-renewable (exhaustible) resources.",
        "Forest, water, and soil resources form the crucial foundation for maintaining global ecological balance.",
        "Uncontrolled human activities lead to severe environmental threats like pollution, loss of biodiversity, and global warming.",
        "Conservation of natural resources is essential for achieving long-term environmental sustainability."
      ],
      "id": "5b4zsxb"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
        {
          "label": "Resource Categories",
          "value": "2 Main Types",
