    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s73egpq",
      "content": "Environment refers to the surroundings in which living organisms live. It includes both living (biotic) and non-living (abiotic) components."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2e57qfz",
      "content": "Environment provides:"
    },
    {
      "id": "kc734t2",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Air to breathe</li><li>Water to drink</li><li>Food to eat</li><li>Shelter</li><li>Natural resources</li></ul>",
        "Air to breathe",
        "Water to drink",
        "Food to eat",
        "Shelter",
        "Natural resources"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "hnzia8k",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "COMPONENTS OF ENVIRONMENT"
    },
    {
      "id": "ezn5kr1",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "6x5kj2m",
      "src": "/books/Guide/GENERAL KNOWLEDGE/images/image_6x5kj2m.png"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d75rajo",
      "content": "Environment has two main components:<img></img>"
    },
    {
      "id": "m292xf8",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Biotic Components:<ul><li>Plants </li><li>Animals</li><li>Microorganisms</li></ul>",
        "Plants ",
        "Animals",
        "Microorganisms",
        "Abiotic Components:<ul><li>Air</li><li>Water</li><li>Soil</li><li>Sunlight</li><li>Temperature</li></ul>",
        "Air",
        "Water",
        "Soil",
        "Sunlight",
        "Temperature"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "z8v6dtr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "NATURAL RESOURCES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fzkx5ty",
      "content": "Natural resources are materials obtained from nature which are useful for humans. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "aaj9687",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Air</li><li>Water</li><li>Soil</li><li>Forests</li><li>Minerals</li><li>Fossil fuels</li></ul>",
        "Air",
        "Water",
        "Soil",
        "Forests",
        "Minerals",
        "Fossil fuels"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gvct1ue",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "TYPES OF NATURAL RESOURCES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mll1yp7",
      "content": "Natural resources are classified into:"
    },
    {
      "id": "7b23wcx",
      "type": "numberedList",
      "items": [
        "Renewable Resources<img></img>",
        "Non-Renewable Resources"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "e8rm49g",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Renewable Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wo0nkgl",
      "content": "Renewable resources can be replenished naturally. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "puznp8u",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Sunlight</li><li>Wind</li><li>Water</li><li>Forests</li></ul>",
        "Sunlight",
        "Wind",
        "Water",
        "Forests"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uc25ln9",
      "content": "Advantages:"
    },
    {
      "id": "rfpba4k",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Inexhaustible</li><li>Environment friendly</li></ul>",
        "Inexhaustible",
        "Environment friendly"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sdqfgy9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Non-Renewable Resources"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g9lnoo7",
      "content": "Non-renewable resources are limited and cannot be replenished quickly. Examples:"
    },
    {
      "id": "tn3fa9f",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Coal</li><li>Petroleum</li><li>Natural gas</li><li>Minerals</li></ul>",
        "Coal",
        "Petroleum",
        "Natural gas",
        "Minerals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k15ergd",
      "content": "Disadvantages:"
    },
    {
      "id": "robp2pv",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Exhaustible</li><li>Cause pollution</li></ul>",
        "Exhaustible",
        "Cause pollution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "19e5lr7",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FOREST RESOURCES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x0h2gg1",
      "content": "Forests are important natural resources. Uses of forests:"
    },
    {
      "id": "rgfp1ts",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Provide oxygen</li><li>Maintain climate</li><li>Prevent soil erosion</li><li>Provide wood, medicine and food</li></ul>",
        "Provide oxygen",
        "Maintain climate",
        "Prevent soil erosion",
        "Provide wood, medicine and food"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gtohtax",
      "content": "Deforestation leads to:"
    },
    {
      "id": "dvadzoy",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Global warming</li><li>Loss of biodiversity</li><li>Floods and droughts</li></ul>",
        "Global warming",
        "Loss of biodiversity",
        "Floods and droughts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "83oklft",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "WATER RESOURCES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4r1ci81",
      "content": "Water is essential for life. Sources of water:"
    },
    {
      "id": "5nxnxo8",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Rivers</li><li>Lakes</li><li>Groundwater</li><li>Rain</li></ul>",
        "Rivers",
        "Lakes",
        "Groundwater",
        "Rain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v9yof5u",
      "content": "Water conservation methods:"
    },
    {
      "id": "k2ohuum",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Rainwater harvesting</li><li>Efficient use</li><li>Preventing pollution</li></ul>",
        "Rainwater harvesting",
        "Efficient use",
        "Preventing pollution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ynlyzx5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "SOIL RESOURCES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "35q1x3y",
      "content": "Soil is important for agriculture. Functions of soil:"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Renewable Resources",
        "Non-Renewable Resources"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Replenished naturally within a short time period",
          "Take millions of years to form and cannot be easily regenerated"
        ],
        [
          "Inexhaustible if managed sustainably (e.g., Solar, Wind, Water, Forests)",
          "Exhaustible and limited in quantity (e.g., Coal, Petroleum, Minerals)"
        ],
        [
          "Generally eco-friendly with lower environmental impact",
          "Significant contributor to environmental pollution and greenhouse gases"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "vw0cvsm"
    },
    {
      "id": "3jworev",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Supports plant growth</li><li>Stores water</li><li>Provides minerals</li></ul>",
        "Supports plant growth",
        "Stores water",
        "Provides minerals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hy2svmc",
      "content": "Soil erosion is removal of top fertile layer."
    },
    {
      "id": "o0zujqm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "CONSERVATION OF NATURAL RESOURCES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wlz5vhn",
      "content": "Conservation means wise use of natural resources. Methods:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ffuw50m",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Reduce, Reuse, Recycle</li><li>Afforestation</li><li>Use of renewable resources</li><li>Avoid pollution</li></ul>",
        "Reduce, Reuse, Recycle",
        "Afforestation",
        "Use of renewable resources",
        "Avoid pollution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gap4sdv",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "BIODIVERSITY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iqbym0v",
      "content": "Biodiversity refers to the variety of living organisms on Earth. Importance:"
    },
    {
      "id": "f68ns0h",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Maintains ecological balance</li><li>Provides food and medicine</li><li>Supports life</li></ul>",
        "Maintains ecological balance",
        "Provides food and medicine",
        "Supports life"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "lbmgcok",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "POLLUTION"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ot7xpdz",
      "content": "Pollution is the contamination of environment. Types:"
    },
    {
      "id": "tl2ygas",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "<ul><li>Air pollution</li><li>Water pollution</li><li>Soil pollution</li><li>Noise pollution</li></ul>",
        "Air pollution",
        "Water pollution",
        "Soil pollution",
        "Noise pollution"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "er5kt9g",
      "content": "Effects:"
    },
    {
      "id": "ogezy4x",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
